## feat(dq): OWL-gated suggest_from_ontology gap closure

Context: `suggest_from_ontology` never used parsed OWL characteristics
(`owl:FunctionalProperty`, `owl:InverseFunctionalProperty`, cardinality
restrictions), so cardinality and uniqueness suggestions never appeared.
The original PR also invented `sh:minCount 1` for every object property
and called the missing `domain.get_constraints()`. Completeness now comes
from class-listed data properties plus explicit OWL restrictions; the
route reads `domain.constraints`. Review fixups applied on `0.9.0`
(Laurent Prat original + review rebase). Extract Function for min/max
count emission.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/shacl/SHACLService.py
   Optional `constraints` argument. Completeness from min/exact
   cardinality and someValuesFrom; maxCount from FunctionalProperty and
   max/exact cardinality; uniqueness SPARQL from InverseFunctionalProperty.
   Property match prefers `propertyUri`.
2. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   `GET /ontology/dataquality/suggest` passes `domain.constraints`.
3. tests/back/core/w3c/shacl/test_shacl_service.py
   First unit tests for `suggest_from_ontology` (OWL-gated cases + URI match).
4. tests/units/api/test_dq_rule_list.py
   Route test proves `domain.constraints` is what the handler reads.
5. docs/api.md
   Document `GET /ontology/dataquality/suggest` with an example payload.

